    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1252">

                <pb facs="1222" n="1056" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1056"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/311</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Fletcher to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-25T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 25, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>270. Your telegram No. 252. My telegram [omission]. Unofficially but reliably
                    informed that instructions have been sent to the Governor of Sonora to leave
                    pertenencia tax matter in abeyance for the present and to endeavor to compose
                    difficulties with copper mine owners.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
